{"name":"Seven Days of Rain","hex":"#d3dae1","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"seven","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["NATO & ICAO radiotelephony clear code (spelling-alphabet name) for the digit 7."]},{"part":"Numeral","definitions":["A numerical value equal to 7; the number following six and preceding eight.","Describing a group or set with seven elements."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/seven"},{"term":"days","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of day"]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A particular time or period of vague extent.","Life."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/days"},{"term":"rain","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Condensed water falling from a cloud.","Any matter moving or falling, usually through air, and especially if liquid or otherwise figuratively identifiable with raindrops."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To have rain fall from the sky.","To fall as or like rain."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rain"}],"entries":[{"title":"7","blocks":[{"text":"7 (seven) is the natural number following 6 and preceding 8. It is the only prime number preceding a cube."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/7"},{"title":"Day","blocks":[{"text":"A day is the time period of a full rotation of the Earth with respect to the Sun. On average, this is 24 hours. As a day passes at a given location it experiences morning, afternoon, evening, and night. This daily cycle drives circadian rhythms in many organisms, which are vital to many life processes."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Day"},{"title":"Rain","blocks":[{"text":"Rain or rainfall is a form of atmospheric precipitation composed of droplets of water aerosols that have condensed from atmospheric water vapor and fall by gravity. Depending on the intensity, rain can be described as a drizzle, a shower, a cloudburst or a downpour. It is also often accompanied by other weather phenomena such as strong wind (rainstorm) and lightning (thunderstorm), and may be mixed with hail/ice pellet, snow (sleet) and sandstorm. Rain is a major component of the water cycle and is responsible for depositing most of the fresh water on Earth. It provides water for hydroelectric power plants, crop irrigation, and suitable conditions for many types of ecosystems."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/Hard_rain_on_a_roof.jpg/330px-Hard_rain_on_a_roof.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rain"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c8/His_Master%27s_Voice_%28small%29.png/120px-His_Master%27s_Voice_%28small%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/c/c8/His_Master%27s_Voice_%28small%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c8/His_Master%27s_Voice_%28small%29.png/120px-His_Master%27s_Voice_%28small%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHis_Master's_Voice_(small).png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b2/Midtown_Manhattan_from_Weehawken_September_2021_panorama_1.jpg/500px-Midtown_Manhattan_from_Weehawken_September_2021_panorama_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b2/Midtown_Manhattan_from_Weehawken_September_2021_panorama_1.jpg/1280px-Midtown_Manhattan_from_Weehawken_September_2021_panorama_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b2/Midtown_Manhattan_from_Weehawken_September_2021_panorama_1.jpg/500px-Midtown_Manhattan_from_We